{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And when you reap the harvest of your land, you shall not finish</b> — This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 23:22): He repeated and restated it to them so as to make them liable for two negative prohibitions. And Ibn Ezra said (Ibn Ezra on Leviticus 23:22) that the reason is because the festival of Shavuot occurs at the time of the first fruits of the wheat harvest, therefore He warned that you not forget what I have commanded you to do during those days. But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that \"and when you reap the harvest of your land\" is an allusion to the harvest mentioned at the beginning of the section (Leviticus 23:10) — it says that when you come into the land and reap the omer, the first of your harvest, you shall not finish the corner of that field which is needed for the omer, and you shall not gather the gleanings, meaning that this commandment does not push aside these negative prohibitions."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:58:21.686127636Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}